# SDK 57 pins react 19.2.3, but packages in the graph (react-dom via expo-router's
# web support, @expo/devtools) declare peers against react 19.3. Strict peer
# resolution therefore fails, which breaks `npm ci` -- and that is the command
# EAS Build runs, so it breaks the cloud build too:
#
#   npm error code ERESOLVE
#   While resolving: react-dom@19.3.0
#   Found: react@19.2.3
#
# The lockfile has to be generated the same way it is installed, or npm ci
# rejects it as out of sync:
#
#   `npm ci` can only install packages when your package.json and
#   package-lock.json ... are in sync.
#   Missing: react-native-gesture-handler@3.3.0 from lock file
#
# So this setting has to stay. If react is ever bumped to a version the SDK
# actually supports, delete this file and re-run `npm install` -- do not keep it
# around as a habit, because it is what hides genuinely conflicting peers.
legacy-peer-deps=true